<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Influence-weighted precision benefit.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the divergence–influence proxy of Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 A Label-Free Signal for Precision Allocation ‣ 3 Task-Dependent Precision Sensitivity Across Diffusion Steps ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, we combine the change in local divergence with downstream influence to estimate the benefit of using precision <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\tau,k}(b)=\bar{\iota}_{\tau,k}\left[\kappa_{\tau,k}(b_{0})-\kappa_{\tau,k}(b)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ι</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\tau,k}(b)=\bar{\iota}_{\tau,k}\left[\kappa_{\tau,k}(b_{0})-\kappa_{\tau,k}(b)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In particular, <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\tau,k}(b_{0})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\tau,k}(b_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math>; positive values favor upgrading a window, while negative values quantify the estimated cost of reducing its precision. This generalizes the window-level signal of Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 A Label-Free Signal for Precision Allocation ‣ 3 Task-Dependent Precision Sensitivity Across Diffusion Steps ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> to both precision upgrades and downgrades. The score is a surrogate for the marginal downstream benefit, not the true change in task accuracy. Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix D Algorithms ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Algorithms ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>) describes the complete label-free profiling procedure.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Optimal Budget-Constrained Scheduling</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">While Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 A Label-Free Signal for Precision Allocation ‣ 3 Task-Dependent Precision Sensitivity Across Diffusion Steps ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> studies the benefit of upscaling one window at a time, our method must distribute precision jointly across all windows under the same total budget. Given the task-specific scores, we solve</p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E5X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{b}_{\tau}^{*}\in\arg\max_{\mathbf{b}\in\mathcal{B}^{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{b}_{\tau}^{*}\in\arg\max_{\mathbf{b}\in\mathcal{B}^{K}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
