<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ A label-free proxy. ‣ 3.2 A Label-Free Signal for Precision Allocation ‣ 3 Task-Dependent Precision Sensitivity Across Diffusion Steps ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix an evaluation example <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and a denoising window <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>,
and let <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the state immediately before the window.
We suppress the superscript <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> when unambiguous.
Let <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathrm{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>up</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathrm{up}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathrm{tg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>tg</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathrm{tg}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the
distributions over the complete commitment outcomes within
window <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, conditioned on the common initial state <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>,
when the window is executed at
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{A}_{\mathrm{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>up</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{A}_{\mathrm{up}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{A}_{\mathrm{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>target</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{A}_{\mathrm{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
A commitment outcome includes both the committed token
values and their positions, and therefore determines the
post-window state given <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a commitment outcome <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{w}(c)=\mathbb{E}\left[m(Y)\mid s_{w},c\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{w}(c)=\mathbb{E}\left[m(Y)\mid s_{w},c\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(Y)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(Y)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is the final task score and the
expectation is over any randomness in the subsequent
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{A}_{\mathrm{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>target</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{A}_{\mathrm{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> continuation.
For a distribution <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> over commitment outcomes, let</p>
<table id="A3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{w}(\Pi)=\mathbb{E}_{c\sim\Pi}[g_{w}(c)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{w}(\Pi)=\mathbb{E}_{c\sim\Pi}[g_{w}(c)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The per-example effect of upscaling window <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta m_{w}=V_{w}(\Pi_{\mathrm{up}})-V_{w}(\Pi_{\mathrm{tg}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>up</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>tg</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta m_{w}=V_{w}(\Pi_{\mathrm{up}})-V_{w}(\Pi_{\mathrm{tg}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">and the average effect over evaluation examples is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{M}_{w}=\mathbb{E}_{i}[\Delta m_{w}^{(i)}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{M}_{w}=\mathbb{E}_{i}[\Delta m_{w}^{(i)}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We define two theoretical quantities:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{w}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\Pi_{\mathrm{up}}\,\|\,\Pi_{\mathrm{tg}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>up</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>tg</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\Pi_{\mathrm{up}}\,\|\,\Pi_{\mathrm{tg}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{w}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{c}g_{w}(c)-\inf_{c}g_{w}(c)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>c</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>c</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{c}g_{w}(c)-\inf_{c}g_{w}(c).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> measures the distributional change in
window commitments induced by upscaling, while <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>
measures the sensitivity of the expected downstream
task score to those commitments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Perturbation–sensitivity bound.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For stochastic commitment laws with finite <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the expected task-score change satisfies</p>
<table id="A3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta\mathcal{M}_{w}|^{2}\leq\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{i}[J_{w}^{(i)}]\,\mathbb{E}_{i}[(R_{w}^{(i)})^{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta\mathcal{M}_{w}|^{2}\leq\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{i}[J_{w}^{(i)}]\,\mathbb{E}_{i}[(R_{w}^{(i)})^{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{w}(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{w}(c)</annotation></semantics></math> takes values in an interval of length
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>, the variational characterization of total
variation gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|V_{w}(\Pi_{\mathrm{up}})-V_{w}(\Pi_{\mathrm{tg}})\right|\leq R_{w}\,\mathrm{TV}\left(\Pi_{\mathrm{up}},\Pi_{\mathrm{tg}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>up</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>tg</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TV</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>up</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>tg</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|V_{w}(\Pi_{\mathrm{up}})-V_{w}(\Pi_{\mathrm{tg}})\right|\leq R_{w}\,\mathrm{TV}\left(\Pi_{\mathrm{up}},\Pi_{\mathrm{tg}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying Pinsker’s inequality yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\Delta m_{w}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\Delta m_{w}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq R_{w}\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\Pi_{\mathrm{up}}\,\|\,\Pi_{\mathrm{tg}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>up</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>tg</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq R_{w}\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\Pi_{\mathrm{up}}\,\|\,\Pi_{\mathrm{tg}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}J_{w}R_{w}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}J_{w}R_{w}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Averaging over examples and applying the triangle
inequality followed by Cauchy–Schwarz,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\Delta\mathcal{M}_{w}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\Delta\mathcal{M}_{w}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{i}[|\Delta m_{w}^{(i)}|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{i}[|\Delta m_{w}^{(i)}|]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\mathbb{E}_{i}\left[\sqrt{J_{w}^{(i)}}R_{w}^{(i)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msqrt><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\mathbb{E}_{i}\left[\sqrt{J_{w}^{(i)}}R_{w}^{(i)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{i}[J_{w}^{(i)}]\,\mathbb{E}_{i}[(R_{w}^{(i)})^{2}]}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{i}[J_{w}^{(i)}]\,\mathbb{E}_{i}[(R_{w}^{(i)})^{2}]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Squaring both sides establishes the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">From <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{w},R_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{w},R_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{w},I_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{w},I_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Neither factor of the bound is available from a single baseline trajectory: <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> compares the window’s complete commitment laws, and
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> requires task scores under alternative commitments. Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 A Label-Free Signal for Precision Allocation ‣ 3 Task-Dependent Precision Sensitivity Across Diffusion Steps ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> therefore uses <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>
(Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In A label-free proxy. ‣ 3.2 A Label-Free Signal for Precision Allocation ‣ 3 Task-Dependent Precision Sensitivity Across Diffusion Steps ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)) and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In A label-free proxy. ‣ 3.2 A Label-Free Signal for Precision Allocation ‣ 3 Task-Dependent Precision Sensitivity Across Diffusion Steps ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)) as surrogates. They are not bounds on <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{w}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{w}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> is
measured along the baseline trajectory rather than between commitment laws, and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> measures a shift in predictions rather than
task-score sensitivity. The proposition thus motivates <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>, but it neither bounds <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{M}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{M}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> nor guarantees its
ranking, which we evaluate empirically.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remarks.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Deterministic decoding.</em> Under greedy decoding the commitment laws are point masses, so <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite whenever the commitments
differ and the bound is vacuous; there the decomposition motivates the proxy without a quantitative guarantee.
<em id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Aggregation.</em> The product of task-level averages in the bound motivates <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. The per-example alternative
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\sqrt{K_{w}I_{w}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\sqrt{K_{w}I_{w}}]</annotation></semantics></math> can rank windows differently; <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> performs as well or better in our comparisons
(Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Proxy signal and aggregation (Table ). ‣ Appendix B Additional Ablation Studies ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Optimality of temporal allocation). ‣ 4.3 Optimal Budget-Constrained Scheduling ‣ 4 Method ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and integer budget <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{k}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{k}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of assignments to windows <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,\dots,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,\dots,k</annotation></semantics></math> whose costs sum to <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>. We prove by induction on <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> that <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{k}(z)=\max_{\mathbf{b}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}(z)}\sum_{j=1}^{k}g_{\tau,j}(b_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{k}(z)=\max_{\mathbf{b}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}(z)}\sum_{j=1}^{k}g_{\tau,j}(b_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, with the maximum of an empty feasible set equal to <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>, only the zero-cost empty assignment exists, matching the initialization. For <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, every feasible assignment has a unique final choice <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}(b)\leq z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}(b)\leq z</annotation></semantics></math>, and its preceding <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-1</annotation></semantics></math> windows consume exactly <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z-c_{k}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z-c_{k}(b)</annotation></semantics></math>. By the induction hypothesis, the best possible value for that prefix is <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{k-1}(z-c_{k}(b))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{k-1}(z-c_{k}(b))</annotation></semantics></math>. Maximizing over all possible final choices gives precisely Eq. (<a href="#S4.E6" title="In 4.3 Optimal Budget-Constrained Scheduling ‣ 4 Method ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), proving the invariant. At <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the invariant is the objective and constraint of Eq. (<a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4.3 Optimal Budget-Constrained Scheduling ‣ 4 Method ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). Backtracking recovers an optimal assignment.  <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
