<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithms <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix D Algorithms ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix D Algorithms ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> describe the calibration and allocation stages of T<sup id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>Quant. Following Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 A Label-Free Signal for Precision Allocation ‣ 3 Task-Dependent Precision Sensitivity Across Diffusion Steps ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, calibration combines quantization divergence at all committed positions with downstream influence. The candidate precisions and resource costs remain symbolic; their experimental values are given in Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Experimental Setup and Implementation Details ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
