<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conventions.</span>
<math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{i,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{i,k}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the steps assigned to normalized window <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> for prompt <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and equals <math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> when all prompts use the same step count. The reference trajectory and all quantized replays use identical saved input states, as in Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Label-Free Calibration ‣ 4 Method ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. We assume <math id="A4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{k}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{k}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for every window. If no masked positions remain after a window, its downstream influence is zero by Eq. (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In A label-free proxy. ‣ 3.2 A Label-Free Signal for Precision Allocation ‣ 3 Task-Dependent Precision Sensitivity Across Diffusion Steps ‣ Different Tasks, Different Timesteps: Temporal Task-Aware Quantization for Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). No ground-truth labels, task-specific evaluation metrics, or score-relevant position sets are used.</p>
</div>
